Using the SAC Library
+++++++++++++++++++++

Overview
--------
In addition to being able to read and write SAC data files in one's own C or
FORTRAN programs (see `SAC Reading and Writing Routines` ), one can use many of
SAC's data-processing routines in stand-alone codes if one uses specific flags
in the compiling stage and the SAC libraries in the linking stage.  These
libraries libsac.a and libsacio.a are in ${SACHOME}/lib.  The .f and .c files, as well as
the sample input files, are in ${SACHOME}/doc/examples.

